"ラブ020 中国のドラマ","ja","alternate"],["미미일소흔경성","미미일소흔경성","ko","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q26205812","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:dance_film","kind":"genre","l":"dance film","d":"film in which dance is a central element in the narrative","labels":[["dance film","dance film","en","preferred"],["screen dance","screen dance","en","alternate"],["ダンス映画","ダンス映画","ja","alternate"],["舞蹈片","舞蹈片","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q3072043","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:mythopoeia","kind":"genre","l":"mythopoeia","d":"narrative genre in modern literature and film","labels":[["mythopoeia","mythopoeia","en","preferred"],["神話創造","神話創造","ja","alternate"],["신화창조","신화창조","ko","alternate"],["虚构神话","虚构神话","zh","alternate"],["神话创作","神话创作","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q3331891","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:video_essay","kind":"genre","l":"video essay","d":"essay, lecture or criticism from a particular point of view in a video/film/tv format","labels":[["video essay","video essay","en","preferred"],["essay film","essay film","en","alternate"],["ビデオエッセイ","ビデオエッセイ","ja","alternate"],["影像散文","影像散文","zh","alternate"],["視頻文書","視頻文書","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q48773471","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:parallel_cinema","kind":"genre","l":"Parallel Cinema","d":"film movement in Indian cinema that originated in West Bengal in the 1950s","labels":[["Parallel Cinema","parallel cinema","en","preferred"],["Indian New Wave","indian new wave","en","alternate"],["New Indian cinema","new indian cinema","en","alternate"],["New Wave Indian cinema","new wave indian cinema","en","alternate"],["パラレル映画","パラレル映画","ja","alternate"],["平行电影","平行电影","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q7134948","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:slow_cinema","kind":"genre","l":"slow cinema","d":"genre of art cinema","labels":[["slow cinema","slow cinema","en","preferred"],["contemplative cinema","contemplative cinema","en","alternate"],["スローシネマ","スローシネマ","ja","alternate"],["緩慢電影","緩慢電影","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q7542092","sitelinks":14,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"},{"k":"genre:kammerspielfilm","kind":"genre","l":"Kammerspielfilm","d":"silent film","labels":[["Kammerspielfilm","kammerspielfilm","en","preferred"],["室内劇映画","室内劇映画","ja","alternate"],["室内剧电影","室内剧电影","zh","alternate"]],"parent":"medium:screen_genres","qid":"Q1502766","sitelinks":13,"slice":"screen_genres_deep"}]$json$::jsonb);

create temporary table import_concept on commit drop as
select
  entry->>'k'      as concept_key,
  entry->>'l'      as preferred_label,
  entry->>'kind'   as concept_kind,
  entry->>'d'      as definition,
  entry->>'parent' as parent_key,
  entry->>'qid'    as external_id,
  jsonb_build_object(
    'source', 'wikidata',
    'license', 'CC0-1.0',
    'external_id', entry->>'qid',
    'slice', entry->>'slice',
    'sitelinks', (entry->>'sitelinks')::integer,
    'imported_by', '0389') as metadata
from wikidata_payload, jsonb_array_elements(data) as entry;

create temporary table import_label on commit drop as
select
  entry->>'k'  as concept_key,
  entry->>'qid' as external_id,
  lab->>0 as label,
  lab->>1 as normalized_label,
  lab->>2 as locale,
  lab->>3 as label_type
from wikidata_payload,
     jsonb_array_elements(data) as entry,
     jsonb_array_elements(entry->'labels') as lab;

do $$
declare
  current_version   text;
  next_version      text;
  old_version_id    uuid;
  new_version_id    uuid;
  ambiguous_before  integer;
  ambiguous_after   integer;
  concepts_minted   integer;
  revisions_added   integer;
  labels_added      integer;
  labels_refused    integer;
  edges_added       integer;
  unparented        integer;
  prohibited        integer;
  links_before      integer;
  links_after       integer;
  rekeyed           integer;
  rekey_ambiguous   integer;
  rekey_hub_refused integer;
  enqueued          integer;
  probe_block       text;
  refused_topic     text;
begin
  select version, id into current_version, old_version_id
    from ontology.versions where status = 'published';

  select count(*) into ambiguous_before
    from (select l.normalized_label
            from ontology.concept_labels l
           where l.ontology_version_id = old_version_id and l.status = 'active'
           group by l.normalized_label having count(distinct l.concept_id) > 1) as already;

  select count(*) into links_before
    from ontology.external_concept_links where ontology_version_id = old_version_id;

  -- -------------------------------------------------------------------
  -- The twin-merge: an import that names a category we already hold is
  -- re-keyed onto it rather than minted beside it.
  -- -------------------------------------------------------------------
  create temporary table rekey on commit drop as
  select i.concept_key as import_key,
         min(c.concept_key) as existing_key,
         count(distinct c.id) as matches,
         bool_or(c.concept_key like 'hub:%') as hits_hub
    from import_concept i
    join import_label il on il.concept_key = i.concept_key
    join ontology.concept_labels l
      on l.ontology_version_id = old_version_id and l.status = 'active'
     and l.normalized_label = il.normalized_label
    join ontology.concepts c on c.id = l.concept_id
   where c.concept_key <> i.concept_key
     and c.retired_at is null
   group by i.concept_key;

  select count(*) into rekey_ambiguous from rekey where matches > 1;
  select count(*) into rekey_hub_refused
    from rekey where matches = 1 and hits_hub;

  -- Refused twins are dropped whole: a heading that reads as two existing
  -- concepts, or as a hub, is not this migration's to arbitrate.
  delete from import_label il using rekey r
   where il.concept_key = r.import_key and (r.matches > 1 or r.hits_hub);
  delete from import_concept i using rekey r
   where i.concept_key = r.import_key and (r.matches > 1 or r.hits_hub);

  update import_label il set concept_key = r.existing_key
    from rekey r
   where il.concept_key = r.import_key and r.matches = 1 and not r.hits_hub;
  update import_concept i set concept_key = r.existing_key
    from rekey r
   where i.concept_key = r.import_key and r.matches = 1 and not r.hits_hub;
  select count(*) into rekeyed from rekey where matches = 1 and not hits_hub;

  next_version := split_part(current_version, '.', 1) || '.'
               || (split_part(current_version, '.', 2)::integer + 1)::text || '.0';

  insert into ontology.versions (id, version, parent_version_id, status, description)
  values (extensions.gen_random_uuid(), next_version, old_version_id, 'draft',
          'The deep screen-genre layer: film, TV, series, drama and crime-fiction classes.');
  select id into new_version_id from ontology.versions where version = next_version;

  -- The copy-forward, restored: the derivation cut it with the layer-node
  -- section and the gate refused the first parent edge, correctly.
  insert into ontology.concept_revisions (ontology_version_id, concept_id, preferred_label, concept_kind, definition, sensitivity, inference_policy, status, metadata)
  select new_version_id, r.concept_id, r.preferred_label, r.concept_kind, r.definition, r.sensitivity, r.inference_policy, r.status, r.metadata
    from ontology.concept_revisions r where r.ontology_version_id = old_version_id
  on conflict do nothing;

  insert into ontology.concept_labels (ontology_version_id, concept_id, label, normalized_label, locale, label_type, provenance_type, confidence, status, external_ref)
  select new_version_id, l.concept_id, l.label, l.normalized_label, l.locale, l.label_type, l.provenance_type, l.confidence, l.status, l.external_ref
    from ontology.concept_labels l where l.ontology_version_id = old_version_id
  on conflict do nothing;

  insert into ontology.concept_edges (ontology_version_id, subject_concept_id, predicate_key, object_concept_id, confidence, provenance_type, provenance, status)
  select new_version_id, e.subject_concept_id, e.predicate_key, e.object_concept_id, e.confidence, e.provenance_type, e.provenance, e.status
    from ontology.concept_edges e where e.ontology_version_id = old_version_id
  on conflict do nothing;

  insert into ontology.motif_rules (id, ontology_version_id, rule_key, evidence_target_concept_id, output_concept_id, evidence_predicate_key, output_predicate_key, rule_kind, minimum_independence_groups, minimum_strength, configuration, status)
  select extensions.gen_random_uuid(), new_version_id, m.rule_key, m.evidence_target_concept_id, m.output_concept_id, m.evidence_predicate_key, m.output_predicate_key, m.rule_kind, m.minimum_independence_groups, m.minimum_strength, m.configuration, m.status
    from ontology.motif_rules m where m.ontology_version_id = old_version_id
  on conflict do nothing;

  insert into ontology.external_concept_links (ontology_version_id, concept_id, external_entity_id, link_type, confidence, status)
  select new_version_id, x.concept_id, x.external_entity_id, x.link_type, x.confidence, x.status
    from ontology.external_concept_links x where x.ontology_version_id = old_version_id
  on conflict do nothing;

  insert into ontology.concepts (id, concept_key)
  select extensions.gen_random_uuid(), i.concept_key from import_concept i
  on conflict (concept_key) do nothing;
  get diagnostics concepts_minted = row_count;

  insert into ontology.concept_revisions (
    ontology_version_id, concept_id, preferred_label, concept_kind,
    definition, sensitivity, inference_policy, status, metadata)
  select distinct on (c.id)
         new_version_id, c.id, i.preferred_label, i.concept_kind, i.definition,
         'ordinary', 'review_required', 'active', i.metadata
    from import_concept i
    join ontology.concepts c on c.concept_key = i.concept_key
  on conflict (ontology_version_id, concept_id) do nothing;
  get diagnostics revisions_added = row_count;

  insert into ontology.concept_labels (
    ontology_version_id, concept_id, label, normalized_label, locale,
    label_type, provenance_type, confidence, status, external_ref)
  select distinct on (c.id, i.locale, i.normalized_label, kind_of.label_type)
         new_version_id, c.id, i.label, i.normalized_label, i.locale,
         kind_of.label_type, 'external', 1.0, 'active',
         jsonb_build_object(
           'provider', 'wikidata',
           'external_id', i.external_id,
           'canonical_url', 'https://www.wikidata.org/entity/' || i.external_id,
           'license', 'CC0-1.0')
    from import_label i
    join ontology.concepts c on c.concept_key = i.concept_key
    cross join lateral (
      select case
        when i.label_type = 'preferred' and exists (
          select 1 from ontology.concept_labels held
           where held.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
             and held.concept_id = c.id
             and held.label_type = 'preferred'
             and held.status = 'active')
        then 'alternate' else i.label_type end as label_type
    ) as kind_of
   where not exists (
     select 1 from ontology.concept_labels taken
      where taken.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
        and taken.status = 'active'
        and taken.normalized_label = i.normalized_label
        and taken.concept_id <> c.id)
  on conflict (ontology_version_id, concept_id, locale, normalized_label, label_type)
    do nothing;
  get diagnostics labels_added = row_count;

  select count(*) into labels_refused
    from import_label i
    join ontology.concepts c on c.concept_key = i.concept_key
   where exists (
     select 1 from ontology.concept_labels taken
      where taken.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
        and taken.status = 'active'
        and taken.normalized_label = i.normalized_label
        and taken.concept_id <> c.id);

  -- A re-keyed twin keeps its own parent: the guard below only parents a
  -- concept with no active broader edge, so genre:apple_2 stays where Apple
  -- put it and merely learns its names.
  insert into ontology.concept_edges (
    ontology_version_id, subject_concept_id, predicate_key, object_concept_id,
    confidence, provenance_type, provenance, status)
  select distinct on (subject.id)
         new_version_id, subject.id, 'broader', object.id, 1.0, 'curated',
         jsonb_build_object('source', '0355_wikidata_headings',
                            'slice', i.metadata->>'slice'),
         'active'
    from import_concept i
    join ontology.concepts subject on subject.concept_key = i.concept_key
    join ontology.concepts object on object.concept_key = i.parent_key
   where not exists (
     select 1 from ontology.concept_edges held
      where held.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
        and held.subject_concept_id = subject.id
        and held.predicate_key = 'broader'
        and held.status = 'active')
  on conflict do nothing;
  get diagnostics edges_added = row_count;

  if concepts_minted = 0 then
    raise exception '0389: no concept was minted, which is not the measured state';
  end if;

  -- **`concept_block` cannot check a genre's parent** — a genre is a block
  -- kind (0190: a term reads as its genre), so it blocks to itself with or
  -- without a parent and the 0198-style null check is vacuous here. The
  -- assertion is the edge itself: every imported concept carries an active
  -- broader edge at the new version.
  select count(*) into unparented
    from import_concept i
    join ontology.concepts c on c.concept_key = i.concept_key
   where not exists (
     select 1 from ontology.concept_edges e
      where e.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
        and e.subject_concept_id = c.id
        and e.predicate_key = 'broader'
        and e.status = 'active');
  if unparented > 0 then
    raise exception '0389: % imported concept(s) carry no broader edge', unparented;
  end if;

  select count(*) into ambiguous_after
    from (select l.normalized_label
            from ontology.concept_labels l
           where l.ontology_version_id = new_version_id and l.status = 'active'
           group by l.normalized_label having count(distinct l.concept_id) > 1) as now_ambiguous;
  if ambiguous_after <> ambiguous_before then
    raise exception '0389: ambiguity went from % to %, so this added %',
      ambiguous_before, ambiguous_after, ambiguous_after - ambiguous_before;
  end if;

  select count(*) into links_after
    from ontology.external_concept_links where ontology_version_id = new_version_id;
  if links_after < links_before then
    raise exception '0389: external_concept_links went from % to % in the copy-forward',
      links_before, links_after;
  end if;

  select count(*) into prohibited
    from import_concept i
   where i.concept_key ~ '(religion|politic|ethnic|nationality|ancestry|sexual_orientation|health_condition|disability|diagnosis)'
      or i.concept_kind in ('identity');
  if prohibited > 0 then
    raise exception '0389: % imported concept(s) name a prohibited subject', prohibited;
  end if;

  select string_agg(probe.term, ', ') into refused_topic
    from (values ('religion'), ('politics'), ('health'), ('military'), ('society')) as probe(term)
   where exists (
     select 1 from ontology.concept_labels l
      where l.ontology_version_id = new_version_id
        and l.status = 'active'
        and l.normalized_label = probe.term);
  if refused_topic is not null then
    raise exception '0389: a refused topic became resolvable: %', refused_topic;
  end if;

  perform ontology.publish_version(new_version_id);

  -- Read back through the vocabulary: the heading the owner named.
  select semantic_private.concept_block(c.id, new_version_id) into probe_block
    from ontology.concept_labels l
    join ontology.concepts c on c.id = l.concept_id
   where l.ontology_version_id = new_version_id and l.status = 'active'
     and l.normalized_label = 'police procedural';
  if probe_block is distinct from 'genre:police_procedural' then
    raise exception '0389: police procedural blocks to %, expected itself',
      coalesce(probe_block, '(nothing)');
  end if;

  select semantic_private.enqueue_recompute_on_analysis_change(
           'ontology ' || next_version || ': the regional tier imported'
         ) into enqueued;

  raise notice '0389: % published — % concept(s), % twin(s) re-keyed (% ambiguous refused, % hub-matches refused), % revision(s), % label(s) (% refused on collision), % edge(s), % recompute job(s)',
    next_version, concepts_minted, rekeyed, rekey_ambiguous, rekey_hub_refused,
    revisions_added, labels_added, labels_refused, edges_added, enqueued;
end;
$$;

commit;
